"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.dev 2303ce843\n- Not reproducible in: 4.4.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev (2303ce843) - Fedora Linux 41 (KDE Plasma) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 (nvidia; 570.133.07) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nA CameraServer error is printed on startup when opening the editor:\n\n```\nERROR: CameraServer is not actively monitoring feeds; call set_monitoring_feeds(true) first.\n   at: get_feed_by_id (servers/camera_server.cpp:103)\n```\n\nIt's printed most of the time, but not every time. If I create a new project, I'll keep seeing it when opening the project when it has no main scene defined, but as soon as it has a main scene defined and I run it, it no longer appears when reopening the editor.\n\nThis is likely a regression from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232. cc @Ivorforce \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new project and open it. The error message should appear in the Output bottom panel.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://a